From: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mpd: fix out of bounds user PD store

q6_register_userpd() indexes wcss->upd[] by pd_asid, which is derived
from the user PD spawn bit as spawn_bit / 8. On IPQ5018 the three user
PDs use smp2p spawn bits 12, 20 and 28, giving pd_asid 1, 2 and 3:

  34: ... smp2p-wcss 12 Edge q6v5_wcss_userpd1_spawn-ack
  38: ... smp2p-wcss 20 Edge q6v5_wcss_userpd2_spawn-ack
  42: ... smp2p-wcss 28 Edge q6v5_wcss_userpd3_spawn-ack

pd_asid is therefore one based and its largest value is 3, but upd[] is
only MAX_UPD (3) entries wide, so registering the third user PD writes
wcss->upd[3] one element past the end of the array and corrupts whatever
follows it in struct q6_wcss.

Size the array so that it can be indexed by pd_asid. Entry 0 stays
unused, and every existing loop already walks ARRAY_SIZE(wcss->upd), so
nothing else needs to change.

Signed-off-by: Johan Alvarado <contact@c127.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mpd.c
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
 
 #define BUF_SIZE			35
 
-#define MAX_UPD				3
+#define MAX_UPD				4
 #define MAX_FIRMWARE			3
 
 #define RPD_SWID		MPD_WCNSS_PAS_ID
